@startuml error_flow_database_failure

title COOKie MVP - Database Failure Handling Flow\nPostgreSQL Error Scenarios & Resilience Patterns

actor "Client" as Client
participant "Controller" as Controller
participant "Service Layer" as Service
participant "EF Core\nDbContext" as EFCore
database "PostgreSQL\n(Primary)" as DB
participant "Serilog\nLogger" as Logger
participant "Sentry\nMonitoring" as Sentry
participant "Health Check\nService" as HealthCheck

== Scenario 1: Connection Timeout ==

Client -> Controller: API Request\n(any endpoint)
activate Controller

Controller -> Service: Execute business logic
activate Service

Service -> EFCore: Query via DbContext
activate EFCore

EFCore -> DB: Open connection
activate DB

DB --> EFCore: Connection timeout\n(no response within 15s)
deactivate DB

EFCore -> EFCore: Retry attempt 1\n(delay: 1 second)

EFCore -> DB: Retry connection
activate DB

DB --> EFCore: Connection timeout\n(still unavailable)
deactivate DB

EFCore -> EFCore: Retry attempt 2\n(delay: 2 seconds, exponential backoff)

EFCore -> DB: Retry connection
activate DB

DB --> EFCore: Connection timeout\n(3rd failure)
deactivate DB

EFCore -> EFCore: Retry attempt 3\n(delay: 4 seconds, exponential backoff)

EFCore -> DB: Retry connection
activate DB

DB --> EFCore: Connection timeout\n(all retries exhausted)
deactivate DB

EFCore --> Service: Throw NpgsqlException:\n"Connection to PostgreSQL failed\nafter 3 retries"
deactivate EFCore

Service -> Logger: Log.Error(\n  "Database connection failed",\n  exception: NpgsqlException,\n  retries: 3,\n  endpoint: "/api/v1/recipes",\n  trace_id: "abc-123"\n)
activate Logger
Logger --> Service: Logged
deactivate Logger

Service -> Sentry: CaptureException(\n  NpgsqlException,\n  tags: { severity: "critical" }\n)
activate Sentry
Sentry --> Service: Event captured
deactivate Sentry

Service --> Controller: Throw ServiceUnavailableException(\n  "Database temporarily unavailable"\n)
deactivate Service

Controller --> Client: 503 Service Unavailable\n{\n  "type": "https://cookie.com/errors/database-unavailable",\n  "title": "Service Unavailable",\n  "status": 503,\n  "detail": "Database temporarily unavailable. Please retry.",\n  "instance": "/api/v1/recipes",\n  "trace_id": "abc-123",\n  "retry_after": 30\n}\n\nHeaders:\n  Retry-After: 30
deactivate Controller

== Scenario 2: Query Timeout (Slow Query) ==

Client -> Controller: GET /api/v1/recipes?q=very_complex_search
activate Controller

Controller -> Service: search_recipes(query)
activate Service

Service -> EFCore: Execute search query
activate EFCore

EFCore -> DB: SELECT ... WHERE search_vector @@\nto_tsquery(...)\n(CommandTimeout: 10s)
activate DB

DB -> DB: Full-text search execution...\n(exceeds 10 second timeout)

DB --> EFCore: QueryTimeout:\n"Timeout expired. The timeout period\nelapsed prior to completion"
deactivate DB

EFCore --> Service: Throw TaskCanceledException\n(query timeout)
deactivate EFCore

Service -> Logger: Log.Warning(\n  "Database query timeout",\n  query: "search_recipes",\n  timeout_seconds: 10,\n  search_query: "very_complex_search"\n)

Service -> Service: Simplify query:\n- Remove expensive JOINs\n- Use LIMIT for count\n- Skip full-text ranking

Service -> EFCore: Execute simplified query
activate EFCore

EFCore -> DB: SELECT ... FROM recipes\nWHERE title ILIKE '%search%'\nLIMIT 20\n(simplified, no full-text)
activate DB

alt Simplified Query Succeeds
  DB --> EFCore: Results (degraded quality)
  deactivate DB
  EFCore --> Service: Partial results
  deactivate EFCore
  Service --> Controller: Results with degraded flag
  Controller --> Client: 200 OK\nX-Degraded: true\n{\n  "recipes": [...],\n  "pagination": {...},\n  "_meta": {\n    "search_quality": "degraded",\n    "reason": "Full-text search timed out"\n  }\n}
  deactivate Service
  deactivate Controller

else Simplified Query Also Fails
  DB --> EFCore: Another timeout
  deactivate DB
  EFCore --> Service: Throw exception
  deactivate EFCore
  Service -> Sentry: CaptureException(QueryTimeout)
  Service --> Controller: Throw ServiceUnavailableException
  deactivate Service
  Controller --> Client: 503 Service Unavailable\n{\n  "type": "https://cookie.com/errors/service-unavailable",\n  "title": "Service Unavailable",\n  "status": 503,\n  "detail": "Search service temporarily slow",\n  "retry_after": 15\n}
  deactivate Controller
end

== Scenario 3: Deadlock Detection ==

Client -> Controller: POST /api/v1/recipes/{id}/rating\n{"rating": 5}
activate Controller

Controller -> Service: submit_rating(recipe_id, rating)
activate Service

Service -> EFCore: BEGIN TRANSACTION
activate EFCore

EFCore -> DB: INSERT INTO user_ratings (...)\nUPDATE recipes SET rating_avg = ...\n(concurrent transaction conflict)
activate DB

DB --> EFCore: ERROR: deadlock detected\nDETAIL: Process 1234 waits for\nShareLock on transaction 5678
deactivate DB

EFCore --> Service: Throw DbUpdateException\n(deadlock detected)
deactivate EFCore

Service -> Service: Detect deadlock error code\n(PostgreSQL error 40P01)

Service -> Logger: Log.Warning(\n  "Deadlock detected, retrying",\n  table: "user_ratings + recipes",\n  retry: 1\n)

Service -> Service: Wait 100ms\n(jitter: +/- 50ms random)

Service -> EFCore: RETRY: BEGIN TRANSACTION
activate EFCore

EFCore -> DB: INSERT INTO user_ratings (...)\nUPDATE recipes SET rating_avg = ...
activate DB

alt Retry Succeeds
  DB --> EFCore: COMMIT successful
  deactivate DB
  EFCore --> Service: Transaction committed
  deactivate EFCore
  Service --> Controller: Rating saved
  Controller --> Client: 201 Created\n{\n  "id": "rating-uuid",\n  "rating": 5,\n  "created_at": "..."\n}
  deactivate Service
  deactivate Controller

else Deadlock Again (retry 2)
  DB --> EFCore: ERROR: deadlock detected (again)
  deactivate DB
  EFCore --> Service: DeadlockException
  deactivate EFCore

  Service -> Service: Wait 200ms + jitter\n(exponential backoff)

  Service -> EFCore: RETRY 2: BEGIN TRANSACTION
  activate EFCore
  EFCore -> DB: Same operation
  activate DB

  alt Final Retry Succeeds
    DB --> EFCore: COMMIT successful
    deactivate DB
    EFCore --> Service: OK
    deactivate EFCore
    Service --> Controller: Rating saved
    Controller --> Client: 201 Created
    deactivate Service
    deactivate Controller
  else All Retries Exhausted
    DB --> EFCore: ERROR: deadlock again
    deactivate DB
    EFCore --> Service: DeadlockException
    deactivate EFCore
    Service -> Logger: Log.Error("Deadlock persists after 3 retries")
    Service -> Sentry: CaptureException(DeadlockException)
    Service --> Controller: Throw ConflictException
    deactivate Service
    Controller --> Client: 409 Conflict\n{\n  "type": "https://cookie.com/errors/concurrent-conflict",\n  "title": "Conflict",\n  "status": 409,\n  "detail": "Concurrent update conflict. Please retry.",\n  "retry_after": 5\n}
    deactivate Controller
  end
end

== Scenario 4: Constraint Violation ==

Client -> Controller: POST /api/v1/auth/register\n{"email": "existing@mail.com"}
activate Controller

Controller -> Service: register_user(data)
activate Service

Service -> EFCore: INSERT INTO users (email, ...)\nVALUES ('existing@mail.com', ...)
activate EFCore

EFCore -> DB: Execute INSERT
activate DB

DB --> EFCore: ERROR: duplicate key value\nviolates unique constraint\n"users_email_key"\nDETAIL: Key (email)=(existing@mail.com)\nalready exists.
deactivate DB

EFCore --> Service: Throw DbUpdateException\n(UniqueViolation, error 23505)
deactivate EFCore

Service -> Service: Detect constraint type:\n- Error code 23505 = unique violation\n- Constraint name "users_email_key"\n- Map to business error

Service -> Logger: Log.Information(\n  "Duplicate email registration attempt",\n  email_hash: sha256("existing@mail.com")\n)

Service --> Controller: Throw DuplicateResourceException(\n  "Email already registered"\n)
deactivate Service

Controller --> Client: 409 Conflict\n{\n  "type": "https://cookie.com/errors/duplicate-resource",\n  "title": "Conflict",\n  "status": 409,\n  "detail": "Email already registered"\n}
deactivate Controller

== Scenario 5: Transaction Rollback on Partial Failure ==

Client -> Controller: POST /api/v1/admin/recipes\n{recipe data with images}
activate Controller

Controller -> Service: create_recipe(data)
activate Service

Service -> EFCore: BEGIN TRANSACTION
activate EFCore

EFCore -> DB: INSERT INTO recipes (...) VALUES (...)
activate DB
DB --> EFCore: OK (recipe created, id=uuid-1)
deactivate DB

EFCore -> DB: INSERT INTO recipe_ingredients (...)\nVALUES (multiple rows)
activate DB
DB --> EFCore: OK (15 ingredients inserted)
deactivate DB

EFCore -> DB: INSERT INTO recipe_steps (...)\nVALUES (multiple rows)
activate DB
DB --> EFCore: ERROR: foreign key violation\n"recipe_steps_recipe_id_fkey"\n(invalid reference)
deactivate DB

EFCore -> EFCore: ROLLBACK TRANSACTION\n(automatic on exception)

EFCore --> Service: Throw DbUpdateException\n(ForeignKeyViolation, error 23503)
deactivate EFCore

Service -> Logger: Log.Warning(\n  "Recipe creation failed - FK violation",\n  recipe_title: "...",\n  step_count: 10\n)

Service --> Controller: Throw ValidationException(\n  "Invalid recipe step data"\n)
deactivate Service

Controller --> Client: 422 Unprocessable Entity\n{\n  "type": "https://cookie.com/errors/validation-error",\n  "title": "Validation Failed",\n  "status": 422,\n  "detail": "Recipe creation failed due to invalid data",\n  "invalid_params": [\n    {\n      "field": "steps",\n      "reason": "Invalid reference in recipe steps"\n    }\n  ]\n}
deactivate Controller

== Health Check Integration ==

HealthCheck -> DB: SELECT 1\n(every 30 seconds)
activate DB

alt Database Healthy
  DB --> HealthCheck: OK (< 5ms)
  HealthCheck -> HealthCheck: Status: Healthy\nConsecutive failures: 0

else Database Slow
  DB --> HealthCheck: OK (> 1000ms)
  HealthCheck -> HealthCheck: Status: Degraded\nLatency warning
  HealthCheck -> Logger: Log.Warning(\n  "Database health check slow",\n  latency_ms: 1200\n)

else Database Down
  DB --> HealthCheck: Connection refused
  deactivate DB
  HealthCheck -> HealthCheck: Status: Unhealthy\nConsecutive failures +1

  alt 3+ Consecutive Failures
    HealthCheck -> Sentry: Alert: Database DOWN\n(3 consecutive failures)
    HealthCheck -> Logger: Log.Critical(\n  "Database health check failed",\n  consecutive_failures: 3\n)
  end
end

== Retry Strategy Configuration ==

note over Service, DB
  **Database Retry Policy (Polly):**

  **Connection Retries:**
  - Max retries: 3
  - Delay: exponential backoff (1s, 2s, 4s)
  - Jitter: +/- 500ms random
  - Timeout per attempt: 15 seconds

  **Query Retries:**
  - Max retries: 2
  - Retryable errors: timeout, transient network
  - Non-retryable: constraint violations, syntax errors
  - Timeout per query: 10 seconds (configurable)

  **Deadlock Retries:**
  - Max retries: 3
  - Delay: 100ms, 200ms, 400ms + random jitter
  - Only for PostgreSQL error 40P01

  **Transaction Behavior:**
  - Auto-rollback on any exception
  - No partial commits
  - Savepoints for nested operations (future)

  **Connection Pool Settings:**
  - Min pool size: 5
  - Max pool size: 100
  - Connection lifetime: 300 seconds
  - Idle timeout: 60 seconds
end note

== PostgreSQL Error Code Mapping ==

note over EFCore, DB
  **PostgreSQL Error → HTTP Status Mapping:**

  **Class 08: Connection Exception**
  - 08000 connection_exception → 503
  - 08003 connection_does_not_exist → 503
  - 08006 connection_failure → 503

  **Class 23: Integrity Constraint Violation**
  - 23502 not_null_violation → 422
  - 23503 foreign_key_violation → 422
  - 23505 unique_violation → 409
  - 23514 check_violation → 422

  **Class 40: Transaction Rollback**
  - 40001 serialization_failure → retry then 409
  - 40P01 deadlock_detected → retry then 409

  **Class 42: Syntax Error**
  - 42xxx → 500 (bug, alert immediately)

  **Class 53: Insufficient Resources**
  - 53000 insufficient_resources → 503
  - 53100 disk_full → 503 (critical alert)
  - 53200 out_of_memory → 503 (critical alert)

  **Class 57: Operator Intervention**
  - 57P01 admin_shutdown → 503
  - 57P03 cannot_connect_now → 503 (retry)

  **All unmapped errors → 500**
end note

